Author: Przemysław Majdak (przemyslvw)
ShortDescription: Automated offline reconnaissance for Burp Suite — endpoint discovery, tech stack fingerprinting, secrets scanning, CORS auditing, and GraphQL schema extraction.
LongDescription: <p><strong>ReconMaster Pro</strong> is a powerful Burp Suite extension designed for automated target reconnaissance. It runs entirely offline to protect client confidentiality and satisfy strict BApp Store privacy policies.</p><h3>Key Features:</h3><ul><li><strong>Smart Endpoint Discovery:</strong> Automatically extracts and groups API endpoints (e.g., matching /api/users/{id}) using a highly optimized pattern clustering algorithm.</li><li><strong>Technology Stack Fingerprinting:</strong> Fingerprints front-end and back-end framework versions offline, checking them against an embedded CVE database.</li><li><strong>CORS Hunter:</strong> Passively audits and detects wildcard, null-origin, and credentialed CORS vulnerabilities.</li><li><strong>GraphQL Schema Extractor:</strong> Automatically identifies GraphQL endpoints and visualizes database schemas.</li><li><strong>Secrets &amp; Credentials Scanner:</strong> Scans for API keys, AWS credentials, and tokens using Shannon entropy and strict pattern heuristics.</li><li><strong>Subdomain &amp; Cloud Assets Aggregator:</strong> Extracts and aggregates subdomains and cloud storage buckets (S3, Azure Blob, Google Cloud Storage) passively.</li><li><strong>Attack Surface Timeline:</strong> Tracks changes in the target's attack surface over time using an embedded SQLite database.</li><li><strong>AI Security Analyst (optional):</strong> Feeds collected recon data into an AI model (OpenAI, DeepSeek, Gemini, or local Ollama) to generate a prioritized attack surface report. Cloud providers are opt-in with explicit user configuration; local Ollama mode keeps all data on-device.</li></ul><h3>Architecture &amp; Performance:</h3><p>Written utilizing the modern PortSwigger Montoya API and optimized for minimum footprint (typical memory usage &lt; 100MB). All network requests, heavy regex matching, and database operations are processed asynchronously, ensuring the Burp UI remains responsive.</p>
BuildCommand: mvn -B package -DskipTests
Artifacts: target/reconmaster-pro-1.0.2-jar-with-dependencies.jar
